   "newText": "This was tiled over all six panels; resulting 11×14 submission was accepted correct (zero wrong attempts).\n\n## Additional verified recurrence (task id `task-05ea8da2`, 2026-10-22)\nThe rule also applies to a grid with a single full-width separator and two panels arranged vertically. Demo 1 was 14×13 with full rows 4 and 9 (0-based) and full column 6, all separator color 6, forming six 4×6 regions. The unique populated seed was the lower-left 4×6 pattern; output copied it into all six regions, leaving separator lines unchanged:\n`[[8,5,0,8,0,0],[0,9,0,4,4,4],[0,8,0,3,4,0],[0,0,0,0,0,2]]`.\nThe solved test was 5×3: row 2 was a full-width separator `[8,8,8]`, separating equal 2×3 panels. The lower panel `[[7,7,5],[5,4,5]]` was the seed; correct output copied it into the upper panel and retained the separator exactly:\n`[[7,7,5],[5,4,5],[8,8,8],[7,7,5],[5,4,5]]`.\nThis gives direct evidence for the minimal two-panel case as well as multi-panel tiling. When all panels are already similarly nonblank or seed choice is unclear, request a demo; otherwise identify the uniquely populated panel and copy it coordinate-for-coordinate."
